# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: silc-free-context
why: crypto_aead_encrypt/decrypt allocate the cipher context (key schedule included) with ae_allocate() and never
why: free it: every call leaked it (LeakSanitizer, CI run 45581879065). The later SILC versions (aes128n8silcv1 and
why: others) free it the same way. The patch frees it before both successful returns.
file: upstream/encrypt.c
count: 2
find: 	return RETURN_SUCCESS;
replace: 	free(cxt); return RETURN_SUCCESS;
patch: silc-free-context-on-tag-mismatch
why: The same context is also not freed when decryption rejects the tag; the patch frees it before that return.
file: upstream/encrypt.c
count: 1
find:             return RETURN_TAG_NO_MATCH;
replace:             { free(cxt); return RETURN_TAG_NO_MATCH; }
patch: silc-free-context-declare-free
why: encrypt.c does not include <stdlib.h>; the free() calls added above need a declaration (C99 has no implicit
why: declarations), so each function that allocates the context declares free() exactly as <stdlib.h> does.
file: upstream/encrypt.c
count: 2
find:     ae_cxt* cxt = ae_allocate();
replace:     void free(void *); ae_cxt* cxt = ae_allocate();
